WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.680
When the news of the bombing came out,

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:06.096
it was a massive story in Germany.

00:00:06.096 --> 00:00:08.346
We are following some
breaking news coming to us

00:00:08.346 --> 00:00:10.388
out of Dortmund in Germany.

00:00:10.388 --> 00:00:12.388
It was covered by all
of the media outlets.

00:00:12.388 --> 00:00:14.138
Three roadside explosions triggered

00:00:14.138 --> 00:00:15.721
at the same time last night,

00:00:15.721 --> 00:00:18.263
as a coach left its hotel
in the south of Dortmund.

00:00:18.263 --> 00:00:19.680
Public figures commented on it.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.430
We should not let them affect
our life whoever it was.

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:27.930
The media echo went far beyond Dortmund.

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:29.388
I think it was front page news

00:00:29.388 --> 00:00:31.805
in every single big paper around Europe.

00:00:31.805 --> 00:00:34.055
Everyone thought of
like a terrorist attack

00:00:34.055 --> 00:00:36.721
and people were scared that
throughout the city in Dortmund,

00:00:36.721 --> 00:00:38.971
there was more attacks to be happening.

00:00:38.971 --> 00:00:42.638
Unbeknownst to investigators
just after the bomb went off

00:00:42.638 --> 00:00:46.096
and the players of the
team were shell shocked,

00:00:46.096 --> 00:00:47.721
the person who had masterminded the attack

00:00:47.721 --> 00:00:50.513
was actually sitting in the hotel,

00:00:50.513 --> 00:00:52.388
eating steak and sweet potatoes.

00:00:58.388 --> 00:00:59.721
My name is Thomas Rogers.

00:00:59.721 --> 00:01:01.846
I'm the journalist who wrote the article

00:01:01.846 --> 00:01:03.805
The Get Rich Quick Scheme

00:01:03.805 --> 00:01:05.805
That Nearly Killed a German Soccer Team.

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:18.221
Dortmund is a mid-sized city
in the western part of Germany

00:01:18.221 --> 00:01:20.721
in the state called
North Rhine-Westphalia.

00:01:20.721 --> 00:01:23.221
And it's a former industrial city

00:01:23.221 --> 00:01:27.596
that's kind of fallen on hard
times in the last few decades.

00:01:27.596 --> 00:01:29.388
It was severely bombed in the war.

00:01:29.388 --> 00:01:32.013
So the center of the city is quite stark.

00:01:33.471 --> 00:01:36.305
Some of the few high points
includes its soccer team.

00:01:39.055 --> 00:01:40.180
My name is Eyk Henning,

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:41.888
I'm a reporter with Bloomberg news

00:01:41.888 --> 00:01:44.471
and I'm a great fan of Borussia Dortmund.

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:46.721
Dortmund fans are super loyal.

00:01:46.721 --> 00:01:49.430
On all match days the entire
city is in black and yellow,

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:50.846
it's like a religion.

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:55.721
I think more than most German cities,

00:01:56.596 --> 00:01:59.805
soccer does play a very large role

00:01:59.805 --> 00:02:01.180
in the identity of Dortmund.

00:02:05.346 --> 00:02:06.555
In October of 2000,

00:02:06.555 --> 00:02:10.430
the BVB became the first
team in the Bundesliga

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:11.930
to actually go public.

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:14.930
Salaries for soccer
players in the Bundesliga

00:02:14.930 --> 00:02:16.971
have gone up very dramatically.

00:02:16.971 --> 00:02:20.680
With such high prices they
thought that by going public,

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:22.305
they would be able to compete better

00:02:22.305 --> 00:02:24.763
with big teams like Bayern Munich.

00:02:24.763 --> 00:02:26.763
Unfortunately, that didn't go too well.

00:02:26.763 --> 00:02:30.138
Dortmund bought too many
expensive players, high wages,

00:02:30.138 --> 00:02:33.055
and the club almost went bust in 2005.

00:02:33.055 --> 00:02:36.638
But the price of their shares,
it has sometimes gone up,

00:02:36.638 --> 00:02:39.555
but mostly gone down since
they made that decision.

00:02:41.346 --> 00:02:44.638
So on April 11th, 2017

00:02:44.638 --> 00:02:47.596
the team was staying in a hotel

00:02:47.596 --> 00:02:50.221
on the outskirts of Dortmund.

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:53.430
Match days are always special in Dortmund

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:55.180
everyone is looking forward to it.

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:59.096
The team always meets in the
same hotel ahead of matches.

00:02:59.096 --> 00:03:00.138
They stayed in this hotel

00:03:00.138 --> 00:03:03.221
in order to have a kind of
a neutral space before games

00:03:03.221 --> 00:03:06.180
so that they could concentrate
be sort of isolated

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:07.971
from distractions, things like that.

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.430
Everyone was pretty
optimistic they had a chance

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:14.555
to go really far, maybe into the finals.

00:03:16.388 --> 00:03:19.305
I was in the office and
getting ready for match day,

00:03:19.305 --> 00:03:20.471
was gonna meet with a friend

00:03:20.471 --> 00:03:22.388
a fellow Dortmund supporter in a pub.

00:03:22.388 --> 00:03:26.013
As always the fans are
very excited about matches.

00:03:26.013 --> 00:03:30.430
On that day, they were heading
to play in the quarter-final

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:33.805
against AS Monaco at Signal Iduna stadium,

00:03:33.805 --> 00:03:35.596
which is in the center of Dortmund.

00:03:37.096 --> 00:03:39.346
Shortly before 7:00 PM,

00:03:39.346 --> 00:03:43.138
the players of the team bordered
their official team bus.

00:03:43.138 --> 00:03:46.180
When the bus took off the
parking lot of the hotel

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:49.763
and turned on the street
there were three detonations,

00:03:49.763 --> 00:03:53.180
three bombs that exploded
and hit the bus of Dortmund.

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:54.846
Three explosions occurred,

00:03:54.846 --> 00:03:57.805
close to the Borussia Dortmund team bus.

00:03:57.805 --> 00:04:00.805
The B team bus had just left the hotel.

00:04:00.805 --> 00:04:03.180
The explosions destroyed two windows

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:05.221
in the rear part of the bus.

00:04:05.221 --> 00:04:06.055
People screamed,

00:04:06.055 --> 00:04:09.013
people jumped to the ground.

00:04:09.013 --> 00:04:10.096
The fellow Dortmund fan

00:04:10.096 --> 00:04:12.221
I was supposed to watch the match with,

00:04:12.221 --> 00:04:14.513
he called me and said "Turn on the TV,

00:04:14.513 --> 00:04:15.930
there was an attack on the Dortmund bus".

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:18.305
And I thought that was impossible.

00:04:21.555 --> 00:04:25.346
Some of the players screamed at the driver

00:04:25.346 --> 00:04:26.846
to keep driving as fast as possible

00:04:26.846 --> 00:04:30.930
because they were worried that
people might storm the bus.

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:34.221
German investigators said
the explosive devices

00:04:34.221 --> 00:04:36.971
used in the attack on
the Borussia Dortmund bus

00:04:36.971 --> 00:04:39.096
contained metal pins.

00:04:39.096 --> 00:04:41.888
One had pierced a seat head rest.

00:04:41.888 --> 00:04:44.430
Unbeknownst to the team members

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:47.055
the actual mastermind behind the attack

00:04:47.055 --> 00:04:49.513
was as they were disembarking the bus,

00:04:49.513 --> 00:04:51.888
was actually eating
steak and sweet potatoes

00:04:51.888 --> 00:04:53.471
at the hotel they had just left.

00:04:54.388 --> 00:04:56.013
Authorities are attempting to verify

00:04:56.013 --> 00:04:57.596
a letter left at the scene,

00:04:57.596 --> 00:04:59.680
claiming jihadists were behind the attack.

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:02.430
Because there had been a series of attacks

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:05.346
by Islamic terrorists
in Germany and Europe,

00:05:05.346 --> 00:05:08.596
there was a widespread
suspicion in the media

00:05:08.596 --> 00:05:11.221
that this was another
Islamic terror attack.

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:15.971
Three letters were found
at the site of the bombing

00:05:15.971 --> 00:05:20.138
that took credit for the attack
on behalf of Islamic State.

00:05:20.138 --> 00:05:21.221
There were however reasons

00:05:21.221 --> 00:05:24.180
to doubt this particular narrative.

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:26.305
It would actually be a surprise

00:05:26.305 --> 00:05:31.638
if ISIS were actually
part of this attack.

00:05:31.638 --> 00:05:34.388
Possibly, could be, employed by other groups

00:05:34.388 --> 00:05:36.430
like the far-right wing to
try and shift the blame.

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:39.013
The letters had some strange qualities.

00:05:39.013 --> 00:05:42.471
They were written in a strange German

00:05:42.471 --> 00:05:46.013
that used big sophisticated words,

00:05:46.013 --> 00:05:47.513
but had basic grammar mistakes

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:49.430
as if someone was native German speaker,

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:52.596
but pretending to be a foreign person.

00:05:52.596 --> 00:05:54.930
Federal investigators
have detained one man,

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:57.180
suspected of links to Islamist terrorism.

00:05:57.180 --> 00:05:58.971
One of two suspects whose apartments

00:05:58.971 --> 00:06:00.221
were raided this morning.

00:06:02.971 --> 00:06:05.555
Shortly after the bombing,

00:06:05.555 --> 00:06:10.930
a man in Austria named
Rudolf, who was a big BVB fan,

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:14.388
he noticed that something
strange was going on

00:06:14.388 --> 00:06:17.346
on the stock market
related to the team shares.

00:06:17.346 --> 00:06:21.388
He emailed the lawyers of BVB

00:06:21.388 --> 00:06:25.346
who then forwarded that
email on to investigators.

00:06:25.346 --> 00:06:26.638
The email stated that someone

00:06:26.638 --> 00:06:30.888
had bought 60,000 BVB put options.

00:06:30.888 --> 00:06:33.680
A wager that the value
of the shares of the team

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:37.471
would fall below a certain
amount, at a certain date.

00:06:37.471 --> 00:06:39.805
Why would someone buy
that ahead of a match

00:06:39.805 --> 00:06:42.221
and then three bombs go off?

00:06:42.221 --> 00:06:45.138
Something, something isn't right here.

00:06:45.138 --> 00:06:46.846
For the person to make money off of that

00:06:46.846 --> 00:06:49.846
it required the stock
to go down quite a bit

00:06:49.846 --> 00:06:51.221
in a fairly short period of time.

00:06:51.221 --> 00:06:54.846
And it wouldn't just be
the team losing a match

00:06:54.846 --> 00:06:57.305
it would require something
much bigger than that.

00:06:59.430 --> 00:07:02.305
There was another big red
flag about this purchase,

00:07:02.305 --> 00:07:04.471
which is the fact that it
had actually been made

00:07:04.471 --> 00:07:05.805
number one on the day of the bombing,

00:07:05.805 --> 00:07:08.888
but also from an IP address
that had been traced

00:07:08.888 --> 00:07:12.346
to the actual hotel where
the bombing had taken place.

00:07:12.346 --> 00:07:14.596
When three explosions targeted the bus,

00:07:14.596 --> 00:07:17.513
carrying the Borussia Dortmund
footballers on April 11th

00:07:17.513 --> 00:07:20.096
written notes left at the
scene claimed the attack

00:07:20.096 --> 00:07:21.680
was the work of ISIL.

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:24.971
The truth as is now
alleged, is remarkable.

00:07:24.971 --> 00:07:29.180
On April 21st, the police arrested a man

00:07:29.180 --> 00:07:31.596
in a southern German city called Tübingen.

00:07:31.596 --> 00:07:33.430
He was on his way to work

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:36.096
and his name was Sergej Wenergold.

00:07:36.096 --> 00:07:38.096
He seemed like an unlikely suspect

00:07:38.096 --> 00:07:40.263
because he had no known connections

00:07:40.263 --> 00:07:43.971
to the Islamic terror world.

00:07:43.971 --> 00:07:46.221
He didn't seem like a far-right extremist,

00:07:46.221 --> 00:07:49.096
he didn't seem like a left-wing extremist either.

00:07:49.096 --> 00:07:54.096
He seemed to be a completely
unremarkable young man.

00:07:54.221 --> 00:07:58.055
A 28-year-old German-Russian
man named only as Sergej. W,

00:07:58.055 --> 00:07:59.930
stayed in the same hotel as the players

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:01.763
on the night before the bombing.

00:08:01.763 --> 00:08:03.846
He specifically requested an upper room,

00:08:03.846 --> 00:08:04.888
overlooking the bushes

00:08:04.888 --> 00:08:06.721
where the explosive devices were hidden.

00:08:06.721 --> 00:08:09.346
The media dissected why he would do that.

00:08:09.346 --> 00:08:10.638
What was his past?

00:08:10.638 --> 00:08:16.721
He had been inspired by the
2015 terror attack in Paris.

00:08:16.721 --> 00:08:18.930
And he noticed that in the
aftermath of the attack,

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:21.138
the stocks of French companies went down

00:08:21.138 --> 00:08:24.680
and he believed that if
an attack took place,

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:27.930
that was directed at a specific company

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:31.096
that the decrease in stock
price for that company

00:08:31.096 --> 00:08:33.346
would be even more dramatic.

00:08:33.346 --> 00:08:34.930
It never occurred to anyone

00:08:34.930 --> 00:08:37.680
that someone would do that out of greed.

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:39.055
We now know that the suspect

00:08:39.055 --> 00:08:40.555
bought three different derivatives

00:08:40.555 --> 00:08:42.471
on the Borussia Dortmund shares.

00:08:42.471 --> 00:08:45.930
With all these derivatives
he bet on falling shares.

00:08:45.930 --> 00:08:48.680
The suspect bought the majority
of these financial products

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:50.388
on the 11th of April.

00:08:50.388 --> 00:08:52.388
The day of the attack.

00:08:52.388 --> 00:08:55.721
If the plot had been completely successful

00:08:55.721 --> 00:08:58.388
and the stock had reached a value of zero,

00:08:58.388 --> 00:09:02.721
Wenergold would have made up to €570,000

00:09:02.721 --> 00:09:06.596
or the equivalent of about $608,000.

00:09:07.263 --> 00:09:10.763
Ultimately the plan completely backfired.

00:09:10.763 --> 00:09:14.180
The attacker Sergej Wenergold
didn't make any money.

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:15.513
In fact, he lost money.

00:09:18.555 --> 00:09:21.555
In court he would be extremely quiet.

00:09:21.555 --> 00:09:24.888
He usually kept his
hands clasped together.

00:09:24.888 --> 00:09:26.513
One of the lawyers actually commented that

00:09:26.513 --> 00:09:31.013
he had never seen a
defendant act so calmly.

00:09:31.930 --> 00:09:35.596
Wenergold had served some
time in the German military.

00:09:35.596 --> 00:09:37.763
From that information
and from online research,

00:09:37.763 --> 00:09:42.305
he was able to figure out how to assemble

00:09:42.305 --> 00:09:48.430
remote detonated bombs that
would do what he hoped to do.

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:54.763
There were a few days of
extremely emotional testimony,

00:09:54.763 --> 00:09:58.638
including the soccer players
who described doubting

00:09:58.638 --> 00:10:01.388
whether or not they could
ever play another game again.

00:10:02.513 --> 00:10:04.096
It brought everything back up

00:10:04.096 --> 00:10:07.471
and it didn't quite help
them to kind of process

00:10:07.471 --> 00:10:08.763
what was going on.

00:10:09.305 --> 00:10:13.055
Throughout it all he
sat there completely silent.

00:10:14.055 --> 00:10:17.221
The big mystery that was
swirling around the trial

00:10:17.221 --> 00:10:19.013
was the question of why?

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:23.805
He may have simply done it because 
he wanted to impress a woman.

00:10:24.763 --> 00:10:29.138
Rebecca is a young woman who
has a very troubled home life.

00:10:29.138 --> 00:10:33.263
She ultimately sees her
relationship with Wenergold

00:10:33.263 --> 00:10:36.430
as an opportunity to
leave that troubled home.

00:10:37.430 --> 00:10:40.846
Wenergold is a Russian
immigrant to Germany,

00:10:40.846 --> 00:10:42.430
he speaks with an accent,

00:10:42.430 --> 00:10:46.013
he has anxiety in large groups of Germans.

00:10:46.013 --> 00:10:50.471
She begins to resent the
fact that he has these fears

00:10:50.471 --> 00:10:51.930
and feels a little bit trapped.

00:10:51.930 --> 00:10:55.513
Rebecca attempts to dump
him on multiple occasions

00:10:55.513 --> 00:10:58.721
and he threatens to commit
suicide if she leaves him.

00:11:00.388 --> 00:11:03.013
Wenergold apparently told Rebecca

00:11:03.013 --> 00:11:05.596
that she would soon be seeing a surprise.

00:11:05.596 --> 00:11:10.596
After being dumped via text message,

00:11:10.596 --> 00:11:13.805
he apparently began planning
for this attack in earnest.

00:11:15.763 --> 00:11:19.930
Wenergold was charged with 28
counts of attempted murder,

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:22.721
which carried a maximum
sentence in Germany

00:11:22.721 --> 00:11:24.471
of life in prison.

00:11:24.471 --> 00:11:26.680
He claimed that he had
nothing to do with the attack,

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:28.305
but as time went on,

00:11:28.305 --> 00:11:30.263
he admitted that he had
actually been the person

00:11:30.263 --> 00:11:34.596
who had built the explosives
and had set them off.

00:11:34.596 --> 00:11:37.971
But he claimed that he didn't
want to actually kill anybody.

00:11:37.971 --> 00:11:40.346
Ultimately Wenergold didn't receive

00:11:40.346 --> 00:11:41.971
the harshest possible sentence.

00:11:41.971 --> 00:11:43.680
He was given 14 years in prison,

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:49.721
but it's still a considerable
amount in jail, in Germany.

